    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d904">

                <pb facs="0854" n="848" sameAs="frus:frus1939v04/pg848"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">390D.1124 Bitzer, John Andre/7: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in France</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Bullitt</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Paris</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1939-12-18T16:00:00+00:00">December 18, 1939—4
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received December 18—2:38 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>2991. Your 1313, October 26, 6 p.m., and my 2690, November 8, 5 p.m. Foreign
                    Office advises that reasons for detention of John Andre Bitzer have been
                    communicated to Consul at Beirut.<anchor n="23" xml:id="d904-f1"/></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Bullitt</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d904-f1" n="23" xml:id="d904-f1-content">
                <p>There is no indication in Department files that any supporting evidence for the
                    expulsion of Mr. Bitzer was ever given; the Bitzers were forced to leave Syria,
                    December 7, 1939.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
